_docs.py` and `tests/test_permissions.py` since the action list changed: 209 passed, 3 xpassed.\n\nChanges, by file:\n\n- **`datasette/default_actions.py`**: registered `create-view` (on the database) right after `create-table`, and `drop-view` (on the table resource) right after `drop-table`.\n- **`datasette/write_sql.py`**: `create` on a view requires `create-view` on the database. `drop` on a view requires `drop-view` on the view's name. A create with no database set is reported as unsupported, as the other create cases do.\n- **`datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`**: renamed `dropped_tables` to `dropped_tables_and_views` and added view drops to it. The spurious `delete` SQLite reports when a view is dropped is therefore not treated as a `delete-row` requirement.\n- **`docs/authentication.rst`**: added both permissions to the `--root` list and added a `create-view` section and a `drop-view` section after the matching table sections.\n\n`SPEC.md` was already untracked in the worktree before I started. I did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1594, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 38588, "uuid": "9e3131d4-3970-4212-9cf7-123e0db63130", "ttft_stream_ms": 1314, "time_to_request_ms": 384, "first_content_frame_ms": 1314, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
